<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<FinalDraft DocumentType="Script" Template="No" Version="1">

  <Content>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="1">
      <Text>EXT. HARBOUR ROAD - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Rain. A chain-link fence runs the length of the frame. Beyond it, stacked containers go up four high, orange and rust.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>A sodium lamp buzzes over the gate. Everything under it is the colour of weak tea.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="2">
      <Text>EXT. DEPOT GATE - CONTINUOUS</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>A guard hut, lit from inside. TOMAS ADEYEMI, 50s, reads a paperback with the spine broken back on itself.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>A car horn. Two short taps.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>TOMAS</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(not looking up)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Badge.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="3">
      <Text>INT. DISPATCH OFFICE - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Strip lighting. Six monitors, four of them dead. MARA OKONJO, 30s, in a grey parka she has not taken off in nine hours, works a keyboard with two fingers.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The parka is soaked at the shoulders. She has not noticed.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>A radio on the desk crackles.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>VOICE ON RADIO (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Dispatch, this is Seventeen. I'm at the weighbridge and the weighbridge says I'm empty.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>MARA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Are you empty?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>VOICE ON RADIO (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I am extremely not empty.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>MARA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Then the weighbridge is lying. Come round.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="4">
      <Text>INT. DISPATCH OFFICE - CONTINUOUS</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Mara pulls a clipboard off a nail. Runs a finger down the manifest.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She stops. Goes back up. Down again.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>MARA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Huh.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="5">
      <Text>EXT. WEIGHBRIDGE - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>A twelve-metre trailer rests on the plate. The display reads 0.00 T in red.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>DEV RAMIREZ, 40s, steps down from the cab, hood up against the rain.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEV</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Nine times out of ten it's the load cell.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>MARA (O.S.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>And the tenth time?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEV</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Somebody's been at it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="6">
      <Text>INT. DISPATCH OFFICE - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>CALLIE VOSS, 50s, night supervisor, comes in shaking water off an umbrella she did not need.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>CALLIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Log it as a fault. Engineering comes Thursday.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>MARA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>It's Monday.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>CALLIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Then log it as a fault and go home on time for once.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="7">
      <Text>EXT. WEIGHBRIDGE - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Dev crouches at the edge of the plate. Runs his hand along the seam.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>His hand comes back wet and black.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEV</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>That's not rain.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="8">
      <Text>INT. DEPOT CANTEEN - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Vending machine light. Mara sets down two coffees.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Dev wipes his hands on a paper towel. Across the back of his right hand, a raised scar runs from the knuckle of his index finger to the wrist. Old. Silvered.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>MARA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>That from here?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEV</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(covering it)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Rigging accident. Different yard.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>MARA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Which yard?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEV</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>One that doesn't exist anymore.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="9">
      <Text>INT. DISPATCH OFFICE - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Mara, still in the grey parka, spreads three manifests across the desk.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Three trailers. Three weights. Three signatures, all the same hand.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>MARA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(to herself)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Same pen, even.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="10">
      <Text>EXT. CONTAINER STACK - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Torchlight between the rows. Mara walks the aisle, counting doors.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She reaches container 4-4-1. The seal is intact. She photographs it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="11">
      <Text>EXT. CONTAINER STACK - CONTINUOUS</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She walks two rows over. Container 4-4-2.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The seal is intact here too. But the number stamped in the lead is the same number as the last one.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>MARA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>That's not possible.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="12">
      <Text>INT. GUARD HUT - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Tomas turns a page.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>MARA (O.S.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Who signed for the four-forties?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>TOMAS</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Gate log's on the hook.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The hook is empty.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="13">
      <Text>EXT. DEPOT YARD - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Mara crosses the open yard, head down, rain running off the parka hood.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Behind her, in the dark, a container door swings a hand's width and stops.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="14">
      <Text>EXT. LOADING DOCK - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Rain sheets off the awning. Two pallet jacks, one dead forklift, the blue sedan idles by the gate, wipers going.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Under the sodium wash the whole dock is one colour.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Mara comes down the steps and gets in the car.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="15">
      <Text>INT. BLUE SEDAN - CONTINUOUS</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She doesn't start driving. Watches the dock through the wipers.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The container door swings again. Stops again.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="16">
      <Text>INT. BLUE SEDAN - LATER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Mara's phone, face up on the passenger seat. A photo of the duplicate seal.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She types a message. Deletes it. Types it again.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="17">
      <Text>EXT. HARBOUR ROAD - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Headlights sweep past the fence and keep going.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="18">
      <Text>INT. MARA'S FLAT - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Small. Clean. She hangs the grey parka on the back of the door, where it drips onto newspaper laid down for that purpose.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="19">
      <Text>INT. MARA'S FLAT - CONTINUOUS</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She spreads the photographs on the kitchen table. Four seals. Two numbers.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="20">
      <Text>INT. DISPATCH OFFICE - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Daylight makes the office worse. Callie has the fault log open.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>CALLIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You went into the stack.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>MARA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I counted doors.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>CALLIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You went into the stack at two in the morning on your own.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Behind them, through the window, the dead forklift stands where it stood last night.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>MARA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Who has seal stock?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>CALLIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Nobody has seal stock. Seal stock is sealed.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="21">
      <Text>INT. RECORDS ROOM - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Box files to the ceiling. Mara pulls 2024, Q3.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Every gate log for eleven weeks is missing its Tuesday.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="22">
      <Text>EXT. DEPOT CAR PARK - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Mara crosses to the blue sedan, keys out, parka over one arm.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Dev is leaning on the wing.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEV</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You photographed a seal.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>MARA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I photographed four.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEV</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Put them somewhere that isn't your phone.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="23">
      <Text>INT. BLUE SEDAN - CONTINUOUS</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Dev gets in the passenger side without being asked. Water off his jacket onto the seat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEV</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Drive somewhere.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>MARA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Where?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEV</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Anywhere with a camera on it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="24">
      <Text>EXT. PETROL STATION - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Fluorescent under the canopy. Four cameras. Mara parks under all of them.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="25">
      <Text>INT. BLUE SEDAN - CONTINUOUS</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEV</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Eleven weeks of Tuesdays.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>MARA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You knew.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEV</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I knew a number was wrong. I didn't know which number.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="26">
      <Text>INT. PETROL STATION SHOP - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Dev pays for two coffees. The scar on his hand catches the light as he counts change.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The CASHIER, 20s, looks at it a half-second too long.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEV</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(under his breath)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Yeah.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="27">
      <Text>INT. DISPATCH OFFICE - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Mara logs in. Her access to the gate system returns a red banner.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>PERMISSIONS UPDATED. CONTACT YOUR SUPERVISOR.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="28">
      <Text>INT. CALLIE'S OFFICE - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>CALLIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>It's not me.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>MARA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>It says supervisor.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>CALLIE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>It says supervisor because the system only knows two words.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Callie looks at the door. Closes it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>CALLIE (CONT'D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Go home, Mara.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="29">
      <Text>EXT. DEPOT YARD - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Mara walks out. Tomas watches her go from the hut and does not read his book.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="30">
      <Text>INT. GUARD HUT - CONTINUOUS</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Tomas picks up a phone that is not his phone.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="31">
      <Text>EXT. LOADING DOCK - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The blue sedan waits by the gate with the engine off and the lights off.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Mara, inside it, watches a container door open properly this time.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Two men she does not recognise walk a pallet jack down the ramp.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="32">
      <Text>EXT. CONTAINER STACK - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Torchlight. Different torch. Two of them.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="33">
      <Text>EXT. LOADING DOCK - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The pallet jack goes up the ramp of a trailer with no plates.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="34">
      <Text>INT. BLUE SEDAN - CONTINUOUS</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Mara films it through the windscreen. Her hands are steady. Her breathing is not.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="35">
      <Text>INT. MARA'S FLAT - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The door is open four inches. She did not leave it open four inches.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="36">
      <Text>INT. MARA'S FLAT - CONTINUOUS</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Nothing is broken. Nothing is missing. The photographs on the kitchen table have been squared into a neat stack.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>That is worse.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="37">
      <Text>EXT. HARBOUR ROAD - DAWN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Mara walks the length of the fence in the grey parka, phone to her ear.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>MARA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(into phone)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Then who does investigate it?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="38">
      <Text>INT. DEV'S KITCHEN - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Dev, no jacket, pours coffee.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEV</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Port authority takes it if there's a customs number attached. There's never a customs number attached. That's the design.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>MARA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>So it's nobody.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEV</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>It's nobody until it's a body.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="39">
      <Text>INT. DEV'S KITCHEN - CONTINUOUS</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Mara sets her phone on the counter. Plays the footage.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Dev watches it twice.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEV</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>The one on the left is the one who signs.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="40">
      <Text>INT. RECORDS ROOM - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Mara pulls 2024, Q4. Tuesdays intact.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She checks the shelf above. 2025, Q1. Tuesdays gone.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She looks up. On the top shelf, a box that is not a box file: seal stock, unopened, forty units.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="41">
      <Text>EXT. DEPOT YARD - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Rain again. Mara crosses the yard with the seal box under the parka.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Headlights swing into the gate. She drops behind the dead forklift.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>A trailer with no plates rolls past two metres away.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="42">
      <Text>EXT. DEPOT YARD - CONTINUOUS</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The trailer stops. A door opens. Boots on wet concrete.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Mara does not move.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>TOMAS (O.S.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>She's not out here.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>A long beat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>TOMAS (O.S.) (CONT'D)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I said she's not out here.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The boots go back. The door shuts.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="43">
      <Text>EXT. DEPOT GATE - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Tomas raises the barrier for the plateless trailer. Watches it go. Then lowers the barrier and walks back to the hut without looking at the yard.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="44">
      <Text>EXT. LOADING DOCK - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Mara comes out from behind the forklift with the box.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The blue sedan is where she left it. Dev is standing beside it, hood down, rain on his face.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>He puts out his right hand for the box. The scar shows.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DEV</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Give it here.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Mara looks at the hand. Does not move.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>MARA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Which yard, Dev?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Off Dev, not answering.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>FADE OUT.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
  </Content>
</FinalDraft>